  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190698/assets/4f0f4b52fc5b84d2d63281da0bc8d92f7433a248550e81c27b0a92a6e5d58a34.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘},$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{CE}$ is a segment, we have that $∠DOE$ and $∠DOC$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm∠DOE+m∠DOC={180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $∠DOC$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠DOC & ={180}^{∘}-m∠DOE \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{67}^{∘} \\\\  & ={113}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
